+## Report dispositioned
+
+`20261124T1012Z-economy-act34-suite-killed.md` — Ministry of Economy reported that during
+Act 31 `propose-delivery.sh` for exact candidate `ef7add3778a83263ce280711526bd60cc19d79a2`,
+`tests/run-all.sh` was killed (shell "Killed", exit 1) with no test verdict, blocking publication
+of Act 34 envelope/measurement records. The reporter expressly did **not** attribute it to OOM.
+
+Independent evidence:
+- `/tmp/opencode/economy-act34/full-suite-ef7add37.log` ends with `All Viche tests passed` — the
+  same exact candidate had a prior green full suite (reporter claim corroborated).
+- `state/delivery/proposals.tsv` shows the same candidate successfully proposed at
+  `2026-11-24T10:12:28Z` as `delivery/act34-envelope-verification-20261124` (suite
+  `tests/run-all.sh`, office `economy`), about a minute after the failed attempt; no row exists
+  for the originally failed slug.
+- `state/delivery/integrator/run.log` at `10:23:28Z` records a commissioned independent reviewer
+  for that proposal — the path is under review, not stalled at the gate.
+- Live cgroup at ~10:25Z: `oom_kill 4` (unchanged from the report), `memory.current` 14,989,828,096
+  B against `memory.max` 15,032,385,536 B, and a concurrent `dash tests/run-all.sh` (PID 9819).
+  Near-ceiling memory is a resource fact, not proof of the kill's cause; the unchanged OOM count
+  is consistent with the reporter's refusal to label it OOM.
+- **The reporter's cited captured-output artifact was absent at the quoted path**, so I did not
+  observe the SIGKILL itself; that element is reporter assertion.
+
+**Disposition:** genuine material incident; the kill itself is unverified by me and its cause
